   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "16e49a3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Cleaning Up Sales Data with Pandas\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** `superstore_sample.csv` — a sales log in the style of the classic Superstore dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "I wanted to practice a full cleaning workflow on the well-known [Kaggle Superstore dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/vivek468/superstore-dataset-final), but grabbing it requires a Kaggle login, so instead I put together a stand-in dataset with the same shape: order IDs, categories, regions, prices, quantities, and so on. Everything below runs exactly the same way against the real file.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you'd rather work with the original data, download `Sample - Superstore.csv` from Kaggle, drop it next to this notebook, and point Step 1 at that filename instead. You'll likely need to rename its `Sales` column to `Price` (or line up a couple of other column names) to match what's used here.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Things this notebook walks through:**\n",
    "- Reading a CSV into a DataFrame\n",
    "- Getting oriented — shape, columns, dtypes, a peek at the rows\n",
    "- Finding and dealing with missing values\n",
    "- Slicing the data — filtering rows, picking columns\n",
    "- Clearing out duplicate rows\n",
    "- Building a new `total_amount` column from `price * quantity`\n",
    "- Writing the cleaned result back out to CSV\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17b0b1b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
