   "source": [
    "## Step 5 — Clear Out Duplicates\n",
    "\n",
    "Order logs like this often end up with a handful of exact repeat rows (double submissions, re-exports,\n",
    "that sort of thing). `duplicated()` flags them, `drop_duplicates()` removes them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "b15dacfa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Found 9 fully duplicated rows.\n",
      "Shape after dropping duplicates: (301, 15)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dupe_count = cleaned.duplicated().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Found {dupe_count} fully duplicated rows.\")\n",
    "\n",
